=Today is {{ $json.asOfDate }}. Here is today's watchdog output.

COUNTS: {{ JSON.stringify($json.counts) }}

FINDINGS: {{ JSON.stringify($json.findings.map(f => ({ priority: f.severity, issue: f.rule, client: f.client, task: f.task_id, staff: f.staff, detail: f.detail }))) }}

WORKLOAD NEXT 7 DAYS: {{ JSON.stringify($json.workload.map(w => ({ staff: w.staff, role: w.role, hrs_due: w.due_next_period_hrs, capacity: w.capacity_hrs, load_pct: w.utilisation_pct, spare_hrs: w.spare_hrs, tasks_due: w.open_tasks_due }))) }}

Write the briefing as an HTML fragment using only <p>, <b>, <ul> and <li> tags (no markdown, no code fences, no <html> or <body>), max 220 words:
1. <p> one sentence on overall status.
2. <p><b>Act today</b></p> then a <ul> of the 3 to 5 most urgent actions, each naming the client, task and person responsible.
3. <p><b>Suggested reassignments</b></p> then a <ul> of 1 to 3 concrete moves from overloaded staff to people with spare hours, matching work to seniority (article assistants suit GST, TDS and ITR work; semi-qualified and senior staff suit tax audit and statutory audit fieldwork).
4. <p><b>Timesheet quality</b></p> then one sentence on vague or mismatched narrations, duplicates or unassigned bookings, naming the staff involved.

